@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
title Valve-switch counterexample (hand-worked, not execution evidence)

participant "Behavior A\n(pump session owner)" as A
participant "Station policy\n(prepare_start_batch,\nauthorize_output)" as S
participant "Behavior B" as B

A -> S : pump session active (ValveA)
A -> S : pump OFF briefly,\nchange ValveA -> ValveB
note over S : Session is retained\nacross valve cleanup
B -> B : sees pump=false
B -> S : request the same physical pump
S --> B : rejected (AlreadyOwned):\nA still owns the session;\nan inactive control cannot stop the owner
note over A, B
A local rule "pump is off, therefore B may start"
would break the session ownership invariant.
This is a bounded station claim only, not proof
that arbitrary composed behaviors share resources correctly.
end note
@enduml
